<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Da Polenta family</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1275">1275</a>–<a href="/years/1441">1441</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as House of Polenta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The da Polenta were a family that ruled Ravenna from 1275 to 1441, and at times Cervia and other towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a>. Their founder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guido-i-da-polenta">Guido da Polenta the Elder</a>, was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesca-da-rimini">Francesca da Rimini</a>; his grandson Guido Novello sheltered the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>, who died in Ravenna in 1321. In 1441 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> took over the city and the family's rule ended.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/da-polenta-family.jpg" alt="Da Polenta family" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_House_of_da_Polenta.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
